  "description": "<p>Which pairs can be the lower and upper entanglement price of perfection for one fixed game? For finite rational Boolean constraint-system games of quantum value one, the positive finite logarithmic dimension-exponent pairs are exactly $0<L\\le U$ with $L\\in\\Sigma^0_2$ and $U\\in\\Pi^0_2$. Every pair has a matched one-way distillable-entanglement realization on the original mixed strategy state. The diagonal recovers exactly the positive $\\Delta^0_2$ coefficients and gives a proof using no $\\mathrm{MIP}^*=\\mathrm{RE}$ witness. For a counter program with polynomial pulse delay, positive lower one-density and one-count $k$, a carry-checker construction gives $\\log_2D_G(2^{-n})=\\Lambda+(m/2)k(\\Lambda)+O(\\log n)$, with the same usable profile, where $m,q\\ge1$ are fixed integers and $\\Lambda=\\lfloor n/(2q)\\rfloor$. At the power scale, every admissible endpoint pair in $(0,1]$ has matched log-dimension, usable, pure-entropy and formation realizations; the dimension endpoint conditions are also necessary. The full usable endpoint ceilings remain open. With linear slope bounds, target profiles computable in logarithmic space are realized to $O(\\log n)$, and sublinear-space targets modulo $o(n)$. Every dimension profile with finite upper exponent is computable within doubly exponential time; some computable bounded-increment profiles with any admissible distinct endpoints are not realized by any game even modulo $o(n)$. This separates endpoint classification from whole-profile realization. The witness-based proof also yields the exact-trace barrier and the projection-minimum classification. In the companion reset model, local-heat endpoint pairs double while joint-reset heat stays bounded. Meyerovitch's entropy dimensions, Hochman-Meyerovitch's local-rule spectra and Sapir-Birget-Rips's time conditions are precedents in form; the invariants here are fixed-game precision costs.</p>",
